WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.900
In this video, we're going to do a more detailed tutorial on Dictation Mode,

00:05.000 --> 00:07.500
how to set it up and how to use it.

00:08.000 --> 00:10.400
Okay, so you can use it simply by holding fn

00:10.500 --> 00:13.500
and putting a cursor anywhere you can type.

00:14.400 --> 00:17.500
Hi Kai, do you have time tomorrow to meet up for some coffee at 5pm?

00:17.700 --> 00:20.500
Sorry, I mean 6pm. Best, Jonah.

00:23.300 --> 00:27.000
There you go, you can see it removed the mistakes and formatted as an email.

00:27.300 --> 00:32.000
You can configure it by clicking Dictation right here on the sidebar.

00:32.400 --> 00:33.500
There's two things you can do:

00:33.600 --> 00:37.000
spellings, writing styles, and replacements.

00:37.500 --> 00:42.500
Spelling essentially is just a list of all the words you want the AI to get reliably.

00:43.400 --> 00:46.200
Then writing styles essentially is just teaching VoiceOS

00:46.300 --> 00:49.000
how you like to write in different apps.

00:49.200 --> 00:51.500
So for WhatsApp, I'd like to lowercase everything.

00:51.900 --> 00:56.000
For Slack, I'd like to keep it professional but casual.

00:56.500 --> 00:58.400
And for my emails, you get the idea,

00:58.500 --> 01:01.500
you can kind of decide how you like to format your emails.

01:02.300 --> 01:07.200
And then replacements is literally just replacing a piece of text with something else.

01:07.600 --> 01:08.900
We have a couple examples here.

01:09.000 --> 01:11.500
My favorite one is definitely the calendar link.

01:11.600 --> 01:13.700
So you can change this one,

01:13.900 --> 01:15.600
and then anytime you say calendar link,

01:15.700 --> 01:18.100
we'll literally just replace it with this URL.

01:18.300 --> 01:20.400
Super convenient to add into emails.

01:20.500 --> 01:21.900
Let me give an example.

01:22.200 --> 01:24.000
So right here, I could say,

01:26.100 --> 01:27.500
calendar link.

01:28.900 --> 01:30.000
And there we go.

01:30.800 --> 01:32.100
Oh, and one last thing:

01:32.200 --> 01:34.700
you can actually configure the button that triggers Dictation Mode.

01:35.300 --> 01:38.100
So by default we have fn, but it could be any other key.

01:38.200 --> 01:41.800
You can do this by clicking at the bottom of the sidebar and then clicking Settings.

01:42.500 --> 01:44.900
Right here you can see the Dictation Mode shortcut.

01:45.400 --> 01:51.300
You can change it by clicking here, adding a shortcut, or editing the one that we have.

01:51.800 --> 01:56.400
So for example, you could have two shortcuts that would actually activate Dictation Mode.

01:56.700 --> 02:00.500
So for example, maybe control option.

02:01.900 --> 02:06.600
And now if I press control option, it will actually trigger Dictation Mode.

02:08.000 --> 02:09.000
Sweet.

02:10.000 --> 02:11.400
All right, I think that pretty much covers it.

02:11.500 --> 02:14.300
If you have any other questions, feel free to reach out to me directly via email

02:14.400 --> 02:16.600
or book a meeting with me here.

02:17.000 --> 02:18.500
All right. Thanks!
